※ pl4g-test: module
※※ A generic function whose arms each call something of this file's alone.

※※ Reached only from the arm a truth value takes.
fn yes(v: bool) → u8:
    if v: 3u8 else: 4u8

※※ Reached only from the arm a whole number takes, with a text of its own.
fn digits(v: u8) → u8:
    let said: str = "0123456789"
    ⎕narrow(⎕drop(#said), ⌜u8⌝) ?? v

※※ Reached from no arm any instance takes here.
fn never() → u8:
    let said: str = "never"
    ⎕narrow(⎕drop(#said), ⌜u8⌝) ?? 0u8

※※ What a value counts for, by its type.
@[export]
fn worth(v: T') → u8:
    comptime if ⎕typeof(⌜v⌝) = ⌜bool⌝:
        yes(v)
    comptime elif ⎕typeof(⌜v⌝) = ⌜u8⌝:
        digits(v) + v
    comptime elif ⎕typeof(⌜v⌝) = ⌜char⌝:
        never()
    else:
        1u8

※※ An instance made in the middle of a body of this file's, for a type the
※※ program asks for too, and one for a type it does not.
@[export]
fn both() → u8:
    worth(false) + worth(2u8)
